-# One batch in the nursery, as a pill linking to its planting. When `pick` it has
-# a tick for planting it out, shown while the nursery is being edited. `detail`
-# is the small text after the name: how many, or the day it is planned for. A
-# plan isn't sown yet, so there is no planting page to go to: `link` is false.
.chip.crop-chip
  - if pick
    = check_box_tag 'batch_ids[]', seedling.id, false, id: "pick_#{seedling.id}", class: 'nursery-pick-box',
                                                       'aria-label': "Plant out #{seedling.display_name}"
  = link_to_if link, seedling do
    = crop_icon(seedling.crop)
    %span
      = seedling.display_name
      - if detail.present?
        %small= detail
